MidoNet is an open-source network virtualization platform for 
Infrastructure-as-a-Service (IaaS) clouds. MidoNet decouples your IaaS cloud
from your network hardware, creating an intelligent software abstraction layer
between your end hosts and your physical network. This network abstraction layer
allows the cloud operator to move what has traditionally been hardware-based
network appliances into a software-based multi-tenant virtual domain.
This page will provide step-by-step detail for neuton integration with MidoNet.
This page assumes an all-in-one configuration. Further steps to configure a
multi node environment can be found at http://docs.midonet.org


== Start RDO ==                                                                                                                                                                                                    
Start RDO as suggested in [[Quickstart | RDO Quickstart]]. After OpenStack is up and running, you can [[Adding_a_compute_node | add compute nodes]]. Later on we'll replace the default openvswitch neutron plugin in order to configure MidoNet to configure Neutron ML2 plugin. 

== Basic Environment Configuration ==

=== Repository Configuration ===

Configure necessary software repositories and update installed packages.

1. Enable Red Hat repositories
 # subscription-manager repos --enable=rhel-7-server-rpms
2. Enable DataStax repository
Create the '''/etc/yum/repo''' file and edit it to contain the following
 <pre>
 # DataStax (Apache Cassandra)
 [datastax]
 name = DataStax Repo for Apache Cassandra
 baseurl = http://rpm.datastax.com/community
 enabled = 1
 gpgcheck = 0
 </pre>

3. Enable MidoNet repositories
 <pre>
 [midonet]
 name=MidoNet
 baseurl=http://repo.midonet.org/midonet/v1.8/RHEL/7/unstable/
 enabled=1
 gpgcheck=1
 gpgkey=http://repo.midonet.org/RPM-GPG-KEY-midokura

 [midonet-openstack-integration]
 name=MidoNet OpenStack Integration
 baseurl=http://repo.midonet.org/openstack-icehouse/RHEL/7/unstable/
 enabled=1
 gpgcheck=1
 gpgkey=http://repo.midonet.org/RPM-GPG-KEY-midokura

 [midonet-misc]
 name=MidoNet 3rd Party Tools and Libraries
 baseurl=http://repo.midonet.org/misc/RHEL/7/misc/
 enabled=1
 gpgcheck=1
 gpgkey=http://repo.midonet.org/RPM-GPG-KEY-midokura
 </pre>

=== SELinux Configuration ===

This guide assumes that SELinux (if installed) is either in permissive state or
disabled.

To change the mode, execute the following command:

 # setenforce 0

To permantently change the SELinux configuration, edit the /etc/selinux/config file accordingly:

 SELINUX=permissive


